   <text:p text:style-name="P90" loext:marker-style-name="T29"><text:span text:style-name="T29">Select the simulator you would like to run on and click </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T33">Start</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T29">. It takes a little bit of time for the simulator to start. If you want to switch simulators, select a different Simulator from the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T33">Simulator Type </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T29">combo box and click </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T33">Start</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T29"> again. It will close the previous Simulator and start the new own. </text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P83" loext:marker-style-name="T29"><text:span text:style-name="T29">Select the project you want to test (it defaults to the selected project in the Apps list) and click on </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T33">Build</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T29">. This will build the app for the Simulator in a separate terminal window. When the build is complete, you can click on </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T33">Launch</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T29"> to run the app in the Simulator.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P83" loext:marker-style-name="T29"><text:span text:style-name="T29">You may close the dialog and make changes to your project. When you restart the Run iOS Simulator dialog again, you will need to Build and Launch again for the changes to be included.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T29"/></text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="P13" text:outline-level="2"><text:bookmark-start text:name="OLE_LINK13"/><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc228354128"/>Installing Additional Simulators<text:bookmark-end text:name="OLE_LINK13"/><text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc228354128"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="P83" loext:marker-style-name="T29"><text:span text:style-name="T29">You may install simulators for previous versions of iOS by launching Xcode and viewing the preferences dialog and selecting the Components tab.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T29"/></text:p>
