   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T10"><text:span text:style-name="T10">You can add App Store Connect users (normally users in your organization) to test the app. There is a link at the left for </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T14">Add External Testers</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T10">. This will require the app to go through Beta App Review.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="P12" text:outline-level="1"><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Hlk74121850"/><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc228354151"/>Apple Privacy Policy<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc228354151"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T10"><text:span text:style-name="T10">Prior to publishing your app through </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T14">App Store Connect</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T10">, you will be required to complete the privacy policy details section. The answers to these questions will be used to create the privacy policy section in your app store entry that describes to the user how you are using their data. The types of data associated with each question is documented by Apple at </text:span><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="https://developer.apple.com/app-store/app-privacy-details/" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link"><text:span text:style-name="T10">https://developer.apple.com/app-store/app-privacy-details/</text:span></text:span></text:a><text:span text:style-name="T10">. The answers associated with the SAB app depend upon the use of analytics and what data is saved if you have user registration defined for your app. </text:span></text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="P13" text:outline-level="2" loext:marker-style-name="T3"><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc228354152"/><text:span text:style-name="T3">Data Types</text:span><text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc228354152"/><text:span text:style-name="T3"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T10"><text:span text:style-name="T10">Under the initial </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T8">Data Collection</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T10"> screen in this section, if the app does not use analytics or user registration, you may indicate that the app does not collect any data. If either of these features are in use, then you should respond that we do collect data from this app. If you answer </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T8">Yes</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T10"> to this question, then you need to specify in the next screen the types of data collected. For an app that has analytics enabled, </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T8">Product Interaction</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T10"> under </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T8">Usage Data</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T10"> and </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T8">Crash Data </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T10">under </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T8">Diagnostics</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T10"> should be selected. If the app has User Registration enabled, then some of the fields under </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T8">Contact Info</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T10"> may need to be checked depending upon the fields you have configured for the user to enter.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="P13" text:outline-level="2" loext:marker-style-name="T3"><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc228354153"/><text:span text:style-name="T3">Product Interaction</text:span><text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc228354153"/><text:span text:style-name="T3"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T8"><text:span text:style-name="T10">This section should only be required if analytics or user registration are enabled. If analytics is enabled, then the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T8">Analytics</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T10"> entry should be checked to indicate that the data is being used to track user behavior. If user registration is enabled, you may also want to check the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T8">App Functionality</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T10"> entry. On the next screen, you should check the “</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T8">No, product interaction data collected from this app is not linked to the user’s identity</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T10">” entry. On the final screen, regarding tracking, you may click the “</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T8">No, we do not product interaction data for tracking purposes”.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="P13" text:outline-level="2" loext:marker-style-name="T3"><text:bookmark-end text:name="_Hlk74121850"/><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc228354154"/><text:soft-page-break/><text:span text:style-name="T3">Diagnostics</text:span><text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc228354154"/><text:span text:style-name="T3"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T10"><text:span text:style-name="T10">This section should only be required if analytics is enabled. The entry for </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T8">Analytics</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T10"> should be checked.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="P12" text:outline-level="1"><text:bookmark text:name="_2tg0gs5dyul6"/><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc475369926"/><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc228354155"/>Building from Terminal<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc475369926"/><text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc228354155"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="P83" loext:marker-style-name="T21"><text:span text:style-name="T21">Scripture App Builder </text:span><text:bookmark-start text:name="OLE_LINK6"/><text:span text:style-name="T21">has a command line interface which allows you to create a new app and build it or load an existing app and build it. </text:span></text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="P13" text:outline-level="2"><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc228354156"/><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc228353930"/>Installing Command Line Interface<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc228354156"/><text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc228353930"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T57"><text:span text:style-name="T21">Choose the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T51">Tools</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T21"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T74"></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T21"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T51">Install sab command in PATH</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T21"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T57">menu item to enable the use of the command line interface. You will be prompted to enter your login password to install the command.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="P13" text:outline-level="2"><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc228354157"/><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc228353931"/>Command Line Interface Options<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc228354157"/><text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc228353931"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="P83" loext:marker-style-name="T21"><text:span text:style-name="T21">Run the following command to run the Scripture App Builder application followed by a series of options described below. The command is:</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T21"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P83" loext:marker-style-name="T21"><text:span text:style-name="T21">sab</text:span><text:bookmark-end text:name="OLE_LINK6"/><text:span text:style-name="T21"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P83" loext:marker-style-name="T21"><text:span text:style-name="T21">The available parameters are:</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T21"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P83" loext:marker-style-name="T21"><text:span text:style-name="T21"/></text:p>
   <table:table table:name="Table3" table:style-name="Table3">
    <table:table-column table:style-name="Table3.A"/>
    <table:table-column table:style-name="Table3.B"/>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A1" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P76" loext:marker-style-name="T21"><text:span text:style-name="T51">Option</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T51"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B1" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P76" loext:marker-style-name="T21"><text:span text:style-name="T51">Description</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T51"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T59"><text:span text:style-name="T60">-new</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T60"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T20"><text:span text:style-name="T20">Create a new app project</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T20"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T59"><text:span text:style-name="T60">-load &lt;project&gt;</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T60"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T20"><text:span text:style-name="T20">Load an existing app project</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T20"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T59"><text:span text:style-name="T60">-build</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T60"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T20"><text:span text:style-name="T20">Build app project (use with either -new or -load)</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T20"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T59"><text:span text:style-name="T60">-no-save</text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T20"><text:span text:style-name="T20">Do not save changes to app (use with -load)</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T20"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T59"><text:span text:style-name="T60">-resign</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T60"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T20"><text:span text:style-name="T20">Resign iOS Template App (use with either -new or -load)</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T20"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P81" loext:marker-style-name="T59"><text:span text:style-name="T60"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P78" loext:marker-style-name="T20"><text:span text:style-name="T20"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T59"><text:span text:style-name="T60">-?</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T60"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T20"><text:span text:style-name="T20">Show command line help</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T20"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P81" loext:marker-style-name="T59"><text:span text:style-name="T60"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P78" loext:marker-style-name="T20"><text:span text:style-name="T20"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T59"><text:span text:style-name="T60">-n &lt;app-name&gt;</text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T20"><text:span text:style-name="T20">Set app name.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T20"/></text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T20"><text:span text:style-name="T20">Enclose the name in &quot;double quotes&quot; if it contains spaces.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T20"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T59"><text:span text:style-name="T60">-p &lt;package-name&gt;</text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T20"><text:span text:style-name="T20">Set package name, e.g. com.myorg.language.appname</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T20"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T59"><text:span text:style-name="T60">-b &lt;filename&gt;</text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T20"><text:span text:style-name="T20">Add book or bundle file. This could be a USFM file or a zipped set of USFM files. It could also be a Digital Bible Library text release bundle.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T20"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T59"><text:span text:style-name="T60">-i &lt;filename&gt;</text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T20"><text:span text:style-name="T20">Include additional parameters file.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T20"/></text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T20"><text:span text:style-name="T20">Use the full path of the file and enclose it in &quot;double quotes&quot; if there is a space in the path.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T20"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P81" loext:marker-style-name="T59"><text:span text:style-name="T60"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P78" loext:marker-style-name="T20"><text:span text:style-name="T20"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <text:soft-page-break/>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T59"><text:span text:style-name="T60">-a &lt;filename&gt;</text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T20"><text:span text:style-name="T20">Set about box text, contained in text file.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T20"/></text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T20"><text:span text:style-name="T20">Use the full path of the file and enclose it in &quot;double quotes&quot; if there is a space in the path.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T20"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T59"><text:span text:style-name="T60">-f &lt;fontname&gt;</text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T20"><text:span text:style-name="T20">Set font name or filename, e.g. &quot;Charis SIL Compact&quot;, &quot;c:\fonts\myfont.ttf&quot;</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T20"/></text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T20"><text:span text:style-name="T20">The font name must be one of the items in the list of fonts in the New App wizard. For other fonts, specify the full path to the font filename.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T20"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T59"><text:span text:style-name="T60">-g</text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T20"><text:span text:style-name="T20">Use Grandroid</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T20"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T59"><text:span text:style-name="T60">-ic &lt;filename&gt;</text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T20"><text:span text:style-name="T20">Add launcher icon (one or more .png files).</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T20"/></text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T20"><text:span text:style-name="T20">Use the full path of the files and enclose them in &quot;double quotes&quot; if there is a space in the path.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T20"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T59"><text:span text:style-name="T60">-l &lt;lang-code&gt;</text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T20"><text:span text:style-name="T20">Set language for menu items and settings, e.g. en, fr, es</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T20"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T59"><text:span text:style-name="T60">-ft &lt;feature=value&gt;</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T60"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T20"><text:span text:style-name="T20">Set a feature, e.g. book-select=grid</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T20"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P81" loext:marker-style-name="T59"><text:span text:style-name="T60"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P78" loext:marker-style-name="T20"><text:span text:style-name="T20"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T59"><text:span text:style-name="T60">-vc &lt;integer&gt;</text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T20"><text:span text:style-name="T20">Set version code, e.g. 1, 2, 3, or +1 to increment the current version code by 1.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T20"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T59"><text:span text:style-name="T60">-vn &lt;string&gt;</text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T20"><text:span text:style-name="T20">Set version name, e.g. 1.0, 2.1.4, or use +1, +0.1, +0.0.1 to increment the current value.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T20"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P81" loext:marker-style-name="T59"><text:span text:style-name="T60"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P78" loext:marker-style-name="T20"><text:span text:style-name="T20"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T59"><text:span text:style-name="T60">-ks &lt;filename&gt;</text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T20"><text:span text:style-name="T20">Set keystore filename.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T20"/></text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T20"><text:span text:style-name="T20">Use the full path of the file and enclose it in &quot;double quotes&quot; if there is a space in the path.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T20"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T59"><text:span text:style-name="T60">-ksp &lt;password&gt;</text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T20"><text:span text:style-name="T20">Set keystore password</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T20"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T59"><text:span text:style-name="T60">-ka &lt;alias&gt;</text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T20"><text:span text:style-name="T20">Set key alias</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T20"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T59"><text:span text:style-name="T60">-kap &lt;password&gt;</text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T20"><text:span text:style-name="T20">Set key alias password</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T20"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <text:soft-page-break/>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P81" loext:marker-style-name="T59"><text:span text:style-name="T60"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P78" loext:marker-style-name="T20"><text:span text:style-name="T20"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T59"><text:span text:style-name="T60">-fp &lt;folder=path&gt;</text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T20"><text:span text:style-name="T20">Set a folder path, e.g. &quot;app.builder=c:\Scripture App Builder&quot;.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T20"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T59"><text:span text:style-name="T60">-ta &lt;target-api&gt;</text:span></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T20"><text:span text:style-name="T20">Set Target API, e.g. 21 for Android 5.0, 22 for Android 5.1.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T20"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P82" loext:marker-style-name="T59"/>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P79" loext:marker-style-name="T20"/>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T59"><text:span text:style-name="T60">-si &lt;signing identity&gt;</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T60"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T20"><text:span text:style-name="T20">Set Signing Identity to use for iOS Resigning</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T20"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T59"><text:span text:style-name="T60">-pp &lt;provisioning profile&gt;</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T60"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T20"><text:span text:style-name="T20">Set full path to provisioning profile for iOS resigning</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T20"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T59"><text:span text:style-name="T60">-bn &lt;integer&gt;</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T60"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T20"><text:span text:style-name="T20">Set build number for ipa file, e.g. 1, 2, 3, or +1 to increment by 1</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T20"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
    <table:table-row table:style-name="Table3.1">
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.A2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T59"><text:span text:style-name="T60">-vs &lt;string&gt;</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T60"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
     <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table3.B2" office:value-type="string">
      <text:p text:style-name="P75" loext:marker-style-name="T20"><text:span text:style-name="T20">Set version string for ipa file, e.g. 1.0, 2.1.4 or +1, +0.1, +0.0.1</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T20"/></text:p>
     </table:table-cell>
    </table:table-row>
   </table:table>
   <text:p text:style-name="P8"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P9">Examples:</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P83" loext:marker-style-name="T63"><text:span text:style-name="T63">sab -load &quot;Mali&quot; -resign -bn &quot;5&quot; -vs &quot;2.3.2&quot; -si &quot;iPhone Distribution: Summer Institute of Linguistics, Inc (SIL) (4YF5X97M4H) &quot; -pp &quot;/Users/builder/Documents/MobileProvision/AdHoc_org.wycliffe.app.mali.mobileprovision&quot;</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T63"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P83" loext:marker-style-name="T21"><text:bookmark-start text:name="OLE_LINK7"/><text:span text:style-name="T21">Running the command line with no parameters will start the Scripture App Builder UI from the command line.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T21"/></text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="P12" text:outline-level="1"><text:bookmark-end text:name="OLE_LINK7"/><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc228354158"/>Using Firebase in an iOS App<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc228354158"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T44"><text:span text:style-name="T75">The </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T73">Building Apps</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T75"> document contains general information </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T44">about setting up the app to support Firebase Analytics, Crashlytics, Messaging and Real Time Database. This section will focus on the steps required to make these features work with an iOS app.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="P13" text:outline-level="2"><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc228354159"/>Adding an iOS App<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc228354159"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T28"><text:span text:style-name="T28">The first step is to go to your Firebase Console (</text:span><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="https://console.firebase.google.com/u/0/" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link"><text:span text:style-name="T28">https://console.firebase.google.com/u/0/</text:span></text:span></text:a><text:span text:style-name="T28">) and select the entry for the application you are working on. Press the “Add App” button, then select the iOS button.</text:span></text:p>
