   <text:p text:style-name="P73" loext:marker-style-name="T44"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P7" loext:marker-style-name="T44"><text:span text:style-name="T44">The next screen allows you to download the config file for the application. Press “Download GoogleServiceInfo.plist” to download the Firebase configuration file to your local machine. It should be mentioned here that if your app has the Real Time Database option set in SAB and you have not yet configured the Real Time Database within Firebase Console, you should either do that first or download the plist file again after that configuration has been completed. Download the file to a location where you can locate it. Later in this section, instructions will be provided for adding this file into your SAB application. After downloading the file, press “Next” to continue.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T44"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P74" loext:marker-style-name="T44"/>
