   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T57"><text:span text:style-name="T57">After making these changes, the provisioning profile for the app should be updated for the new capability and the entry updated in SAB.</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T57"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P110" loext:marker-style-name="T57"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T57"><text:span text:style-name="T57">For Firebase to send notification to the app, it will need to have a key uploaded to it. The preferred manner is to go to the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T71">Keys </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T57">section in Apple Developer and select to create an Apple Push Notifications service key, using the first option on the screen below. One key of this type is created to be used with all apps associated with this organization. If a key has already been created, then use that. </text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard" loext:marker-style-name="T57"><draw:frame draw:style-name="fr1" draw:name="Picture 50" text:anchor-type="as-char" svg:width="6.2638in" svg:height="4.1354in" draw:z-index="0"><draw:image draw:mime-type="image/png">
